The `testBackends()` function declared a return type requiring `available`, `latency`, and `error` properties, but only provided them conditionally:

```typescript
// Before - missing properties
if (response.ok) {
  results.vercel = { available: true, latency };  // missing 'error'
}
catch (error: any) {
  results.vercel = { available: false, error: ... };  // missing 'latency'
}

// After - all properties present
if (response.ok) {
  results.vercel = { available: true, latency, error: '' };
}
catch (error: any) {
  results.vercel = { available: false, error: ..., latency: 0 };
}
```

Applied same fix to both vercel and render backend tests.

