Added a new GitHub integration action that allows sending a raw query to GitHub's GraphQL API. The output is of type `unknown`, but you can map it to a type pretty safely and easily like so:
```typescript
const query = `
  query FindFirstIssue($login: String!) {
    organization(login: $login) {
      repositories(first: 100) {
        nodes {
          id
          name
        }
      }
    }
  }`;

const {
  output: { result },
} = await props.client.callAction({
  type: "github:sendRawGraphqlQuery",
  input: {
    query: query,
    parameters: {
      login: "botpress",
    },
  },
});

const parsed = result as {
  organization: {
    repositories: {
      nodes: {
        id: string;
        name: string;
      }[];
    };
  };
};

const repos = parsed.organization.repositories.nodes;
console.log(repos.map((repo) => repo.name));
```

